## 2. Why arithmetic independence needs four beams

The positive half of independence uses derivability conditions, consistency of arithmetic, and reflection. The negative half uses classical reasoning and contradiction-proof soundness.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

{{visualization:1}}

<details><summary>Reveal both proof halves</summary>
If arithmetic proved $\operatorname{Con}(T)$, reflection would give $\operatorname{Con}(\mathrm{PA})$, contradicting second incompleteness. If arithmetic proved $
eg\operatorname{Con}(T)$, double-negation elimination would give $\Box_T ot$, contradicting the soundness condition.
</details>

